{"qid":"Q221","names":["Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia"],"title":"Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia","endonym":{"native":"Република Северна Македонија","lang":"mk"},"capsule":"The Republic of Macedonia declared independence from Yugoslavia following a referendum on 8 September 1991 and joined the United Nations in 1993, but was admitted under the provisional designation 'Former Yugoslav Republic of Macedonia' (FYROM) due to Greek objections over the name's implied claim to the broader Macedonian region. Greece imposed a trade embargo in 1994–1995 and blocked NATO and EU accession under the FYROM designation for over two decades. The 2018 Prespa Agreement between Prime Ministers Zoran Zaev and Alexis Tsipras resolved the dispute, and the country's constitution was amended to 'Republic of North Macedonia,' entering force on 12 February 2019, after which it joined NATO in 2020.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Borders are internationally recognized with high cartographic precision; the territorial record is unambiguous for this period.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: North Macedonia","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/North-Macedonia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: North Macedonia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Macedonia"}],"britannica":"place/North-Macedonia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"North Macedonia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q153381","name":"Kiro Gligorov","start":1991,"end":1999,"image":"Киро Глигоров 03 (28-01-1993).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%D0%9A%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%BE%20%D0%93%D0%BB%D0%B8%D0%B3%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%2003%20(28-01-1993).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"European Commission","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Киро Глигоров","nativeLang":"mk"},{"qid":"Q1990673","name":"Nikola Kljusev","start":1991,"end":1992,"image":null,"nativeName":"Никола Кљусев","nativeLang":"mk"},{"qid":"Q956519","name":"Ljubčo Georgievski","start":1998,"end":2002,"image":"Ljubčo Georgievski.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ljub%C4%8Do%20Georgievski.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"European Commission","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Љупчо Георгиевски","nativeLang":"mk"},{"qid":"Q237782","name":"Boris Trajkovski","start":1999,"end":2004,"image":"Борис Трайковский (07-03-2002) (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/%D0%91%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B8%D1%81%20%D0%A2%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9%20(07-03-2002)%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"Christian Lambiotte / European Communities","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Борис Трајковски","nativeLang":"mk"},{"qid":"Q157111","name":"Branko Crvenkovski","start":2004,"end":2009,"image":"Branko Crvenkovski (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Branko%20Crvenkovski%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY 4.0","artist":"European Commission","attributionRequired":true},"nativeName":"Бранко Црвенковски","nativeLang":"mk"},{"qid":"Q1363047","name":"Ljupčo Jordanovski","start":2004,"end":2004,"image":null,"nativeName":"Љупчо Јордановски","nativeLang":"mk"},{"qid":"Q162983","name":"Radmila Šekerinska","start":2004,"end":2004,"image":"Radmila Shekerinska official portrait 2020 (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Radmila%20Shekerinska%20official%20portrait%202020%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","artist":"Government of